Scene: VirtualGeometrySkinned.olo
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Skinned virtualized geometry (issue #1150) — a rigged character drawn through
# the Nanite-style cluster LOD DAG.
#
# REQUIRES THE DEFERRED RENDERING PATH, like every virtual-geometry scene:
# VirtualGeometryPass self-disables on Forward / Forward+. On load:
# Renderer Settings -> Rendering Path -> Deferred. (The Virtual Mesh inspector
# shows a warning plus a one-click switch while the wrong path is active.)
#
# PRESS PLAY.
#
# ⚠ TODAY THE TWO VIRTUAL CHARACTERS STAND IN THEIR BIND POSE AND THE CLASSIC
#   ONE WALKS — see issue #1272, and this scene is its reproduction.
#
#   Nothing is wrong with the renderer: a VirtualMeshComponent addresses its
#   mesh by AssetHandle, and no MeshSource ASSET in the engine carries bone
#   influences, because the asset import path (Model + CreateCombinedMeshSource)
#   never extracted them. Only AnimatedModel does, which is what the classic
#   character's MeshComponent holds — hence one walking figure and two T-posed
#   ones from the same file. OloEngine.log says exactly this, once per mesh:
#   "submitted with a bone palette but no part of its cooked cluster DAG
#   carries a skinning payload — it renders in its REST POSE".
#
#   When #1272 lands, all three animate and this becomes the live demo of
#   skinned virtual geometry. The renderer half is already proven headlessly by
#   VirtualSkinnedBoundsTest and by
#   VirtualGeometryVisualEvidence.ASkinnedVirtualMeshDeformsOnScreenFromEveryAngle,
#   which drive this same pipeline from a procedurally rigged MeshSource.
#
# WHAT EACH ENTITY IS FOR
#
#   * "CesiumMan (virtual, skinned)" — the subject. A VirtualMeshComponent and a
#     SkeletonComponent on the same entity is what makes a virtual mesh skinned;
#     the AnimationStateComponent drives the skeleton the virtual path reads.
#     4,672 triangles over 19 joints.
#   * "CesiumMan (classic, skinned)" — the CONTROL, three units to the left,
#     drawn by the ordinary skinned mesh path from the same file and the same
#     animation. The two must move identically. This is the comparison that
#     separates "the deformation is wrong" from "the whole scene is wrong", and
#     it is the reason the scene has two characters rather than one.
#   * "CesiumMan (virtual, coarse cut)" — the same subject again at an error
#     threshold of 16 px instead of 0.5, so the DAG cut collapses toward the
#     root clusters WHILE deforming. A crack or a hole here and not on the fine
#     one means the conservative bounds stopped holding at a coarse level, which
#     is the failure docs/agent-rules/deforming-geometry-conservative-bounds.md
#     is about.
#
# The ground plane is a classic mesh, so the characters' shadows land on
# geometry the virtual path did not draw — a deformed shadow on it is the
# shadow-depth stage reading the same pose as the G-Buffer.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Entities:
  - Entity: 810000000000001
    TagComponent:
      Tag: Camera
    TransformComponent:
      Translation: [0, 1.1, 4.2]
      Rotation: [-0.08, 0, 0]
      Scale: [1, 1, 1]
    CameraComponent:
      Camera:
        ProjectionType: 0
        PerspectiveFOV: 0.785398185
        PerspectiveNear: 0.1
        PerspectiveFar: 500
        OrthographicSize: 10
        OrthographicNear: -1
        OrthographicFar: 1
      Primary: true
      FixedAspectRatio: false
  - Entity: 810000000000002
    TagComponent:
      Tag: Skybox
    TransformComponent:
      Translation: [0, 0, 0]
      Rotation: [0, 0, 0]
      Scale: [1, 1, 1]
    EnvironmentMapComponent:
      FilePath: assets/textures/hdr/newport_loft.hdr
      IsCubemapFolder: false
  - Entity: 810000000000003
    TagComponent:
      Tag: Sun
    TransformComponent:
      Translation: [0, 12, 0]
      Rotation: [0, 0, 0]
      Scale: [1, 1, 1]
    DirectionalLightComponent:
      Direction: [-0.35, -0.8, -0.45]
      Color: [1, 0.96, 0.88]
      Intensity: 5
      CastShadows: true
      ShadowDepthBiasTexels: 2
      ShadowNormalBias: 0.01
      MaxShadowDistance: 300
      CascadeSplitLambda: 0.92
  - Entity: 810000000000004
    TagComponent:
      Tag: Ground Plane
    TransformComponent:
      Translation: [0, -0.02, 0]
      Rotation: [0, 0, 0]
      Scale: [40, 0.04, 40]
    MeshComponent:
      Primitive: 1
    MaterialComponent:
      AlbedoColor: [0.32, 0.33, 0.35]
      Metallic: 0
      Roughness: 0.9

  # ═══ The subject: a skinned mesh through the virtualized path ═══
  - Entity: 810000000000010
    TagComponent:
      Tag: CesiumMan (virtual, skinned)
    TransformComponent:
      Translation: [0, 0, 0]
      Rotation: [0, 0, 0]
      Scale: [1, 1, 1]
    VirtualMeshComponent:
      Enabled: true
      MeshSource: 4896684622676915332
      ErrorThresholdPixels: 0.5
      CastShadows: true
    MaterialComponent:
      AlbedoColor: [0.85, 0.78, 0.7]
      Metallic: 0
      Roughness: 0.65
    AnimationStateComponent:
      State: 0
      CurrentTime: 0
      BlendDuration: 0.3
      CurrentClipIndex: 0
      IsPlaying: true
      SourceFilePath: Models/CesiumMan/CesiumMan.gltf
      CurrentClipName: ""
    SkeletonComponent:
      {}

  # ═══ The control: the SAME file and animation, drawn the classic way ═══
  - Entity: 810000000000011
    TagComponent:
      Tag: CesiumMan (classic, skinned)
    TransformComponent:
      Translation: [-1.6, 0, 0]
      Rotation: [0, 0, 0]
      Scale: [1, 1, 1]
    MeshComponent:
      {}
    MaterialComponent:
      AlbedoColor: [0.62, 0.72, 0.85]
      Metallic: 0
      Roughness: 0.65
    AnimationStateComponent:
      State: 0
      CurrentTime: 0
      BlendDuration: 0.3
      CurrentClipIndex: 0
      IsPlaying: true
      SourceFilePath: Models/CesiumMan/CesiumMan.gltf
      CurrentClipName: ""
    SkeletonComponent:
      {}

  # ═══ The same subject at a COARSE cut, still deforming ═══
  - Entity: 810000000000012
    TagComponent:
      Tag: CesiumMan (virtual, coarse cut)
    TransformComponent:
      Translation: [1.6, 0, 0]
      Rotation: [0, 0, 0]
      Scale: [1, 1, 1]
    VirtualMeshComponent:
      Enabled: true
      MeshSource: 4896684622676915332
      ErrorThresholdPixels: 16
      CastShadows: true
    MaterialComponent:
      AlbedoColor: [0.85, 0.6, 0.45]
      Metallic: 0
      Roughness: 0.65
    AnimationStateComponent:
      State: 0
      CurrentTime: 0
      BlendDuration: 0.3
      CurrentClipIndex: 0
